# {{appName}} SDK - AI Agent Reference

## Installation

Add to your `Package.swift`:

```swift
dependencies: [
    .package(url: "https://github.com/your-org/{{packageName}}", from: "{{packageVersion}}")
]
```

Then add `{{packageName}}` as a dependency of your target.

## Quick Start

```swift
import {{packageName}}

let client = {{clientClassName}}(host: "https://api.example.com", accessToken: "your-token")
```

## Authentication

All authentication is handled via `Authenticator` protocol implementations passed to the client initializer.

### Bearer Token

```swift
let authenticator = BearerAuthenticator(host: "https://api.example.com", token: "your-token")
let client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator: authenticator)
```

{{#hasBasicAuth}}
### Basic Auth

```swift
let authenticator = BasicAuthenticator(host: "https://api.example.com", username: "username", password: "password")
let client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator: authenticator)
```

{{/hasBasicAuth}}
{{#hasApiKeyAuth}}
### API Key

```swift
let authenticator = ApiKeyAuthenticator(host: "https://api.example.com", keyName: "key-name", keyValue: "key-value", location: .header)
let client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator: authenticator)
```

{{/hasApiKeyAuth}}
{{#hasOAuth2ClientCredentials}}
### OAuth2 Client Credentials

```swift
let authenticator = OAuth2ClientCredentialsAuthenticator(
    host: "https://api.example.com",
    clientId: "client-id",
    clientSecret: "client-secret",
    tokenUrl: "https://auth.example.com/token")
let client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator: authenticator)
```

